1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,861
This is an amino-chain.

2
00:00:01,861 --> 00:00:07,031
It is just amino acids, linked one after another, like beads on a string.

3
00:00:07,031 --> 00:00:09,713
One amino acid alone does not do much.

4
00:00:09,713 --> 00:00:12,408
Link a few together, and you have a peptide.

5
00:00:12,408 --> 00:00:16,263
Keep linking more, and at some point, it becomes a protein.

6
00:00:16,263 --> 00:00:18,528
Same building blocks, every time.

7
00:00:18,528 --> 00:00:23,085
The only real difference is how many links there are, and the order they come in.

8
00:00:23,085 --> 00:00:25,091
A short chain: peptide.

9
00:00:25,091 --> 00:00:27,187
A long chain: protein.

10
00:00:27,187 --> 00:00:28,580
That is the whole idea.

11
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,507
Follow for more peptide math.

